      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To respect the diverse perspectives within our firm without compromising the professional atmosphere, the following policy applies to \"Political Expression in the Workplace\":\n\n1. **Non-Professional Discussion Zones:** Political discussions are permitted in dedicated spaces like lounges or during breaks, ensuring they occur outside work hours and away from professional environments.\n\n2. **Respect Boundaries:** Employees must refrain from engaging in political debates during work hours in common areas to maintain a professional, inclusive workplace.\n\n3. **Equality and Non-Discrimination:** All political views must be respected; employees must treat colleagues with dignity and refrain from behaviors that undermine workplace cohesion or create a hostile environment.\n\n4. **Conflict of Interest:** Discussions or actions involving political activities or affiliations during work hours may be seen as a conflict of interest and could lead to corrective measures in extreme cases.\n\n5. **Informal Educational Discourse:** Employees may bring up political issues for educational learning or to enhance understanding within moderation, without crossing into debates that could incite discord.\n\n6. **Liberty of Expression Policy:** Employees retain their rights to express their political beliefs but must differentiate personal dialogues from professional interactions.\n\nWe trust this policy will nurture an inclusive atmosphere conducive to collaboration and respect. HR is here to address any concerns about this policy's",
